get_defs {"success": true, "message": "9 of 9 def(s) resolved", "requested": 9, "foundCount": 9, "notFound": [], "malformed": [], "fieldsAsked": ["description"], "defs": [{"requested": "ThingDef/RM_FurnaceBeast", "found": true, "defName": "RM_FurnaceBeast", "defType": "ThingDef", "label": "furnace-beast", "modName": "RimMandrake: Baroque Biomes", "packageId": "mandrake.rm.biomes", "fields": {"description": "A giant whose banded mineral hide stores the heat of the burns and glows between the plates. It walks into the flames to bank that heat, and carries it long after. A kept furnace-beast can heat a barn for weeks, but may also set the floor alight."}}, {"requested": "ThingDef/RM_Ashwallow", "found": true, "defName": "RM_Ashwallow", "defType": "ThingDef", "label": "ashwallow", "modName": "RimMandrake: Baroque Biomes", "packageId": "mandrake.rm.biomes", "fields": {"description": "A low, broad grazer with cracked ash-grey plates, a spade-shaped face and blunt teeth for digging up roots. Ahead of a fire it digs in and folds its legs beneath the body, sealing itself into a smooth dome. It emerges after the ground cools to feed on fresh regrowth."}}, {"requested": "ThingDef/RM_FireHawk", "found": true, "defName": "RM_FireHawk", "defType": "ThingDef", "label": "fire-hawk", "modName": "RimMandrake: Baroque Biomes", "packageId": "mandrake.rm.biomes", "fields": {"description": "A lean raptor of the standing burn, ash-grey and ember-orange, that flushes prey ahead of the flame-line and is said to carry a burning twig from one fire to the next when the burn stalls. The Pyrelands' first igniter with wings."}}, {"requested": "ThingDef/RM_Flamefang", "found": true, "defName": "RM_Flamefang", "defType": "ThingDef", "label": "flamefang", "modName": "RimMandrake: Baroque Biomes", "packageId": "mandrake.rm.biomes", "fields": {"description": "A venomous serpent that shelters in the smouldering root-mat ahead of a grass fire. It waits for the heat to flush small prey from cover, then strikes from the ash; its venom causes a lingering burning pain."}}, {"requested": "ThingDef/RM_Ullai", "found": true, "defName": "RM_Ullai", "defType": "ThingDef", "label": "ullai", "modName": "RimMandrake: Baroque Biomes", "packageId": "mandrake.rm.biomes", "fields": {"description": "A tall, light-boned grazer with an ash-grey back, soot-cream belly and black lower legs. Its herds follow burns a few days old, cropping fresh shoots close to the ash. Patient handlers can tame them for meat and hides."}}, 
DESCRIPTIONS {"RM_FurnaceBeast": "A giant whose banded mineral hide stores the heat of the burns and glows between the plates. It walks into the flames to bank that heat, and carries it long after. A kept furnace-beast can heat a barn for weeks, but may also set the floor alight.", "RM_Ashwallow": "A low, broad grazer with cracked ash-grey plates, a spade-shaped face and blunt teeth for digging up roots. Ahead of a fire it digs in and folds its legs beneath the body, sealing itself into a smooth dome. It emerges after the ground cools to feed on fresh regrowth.", "RM_FireHawk": "A lean raptor of the standing burn, ash-grey and ember-orange, that flushes prey ahead of the flame-line and is said to carry a burning twig from one fire to the next when the burn stalls. The Pyrelands' first igniter with wings.", "RM_Flamefang": "A venomous serpent that shelters in the smouldering root-mat ahead of a grass fire. It waits for the heat to flush small prey from cover, then strikes from the ash; its venom causes a lingering burning pain.", "RM_Ullai": "A tall, light-boned grazer with an ash-grey back, soot-cream belly and black lower legs. Its herds follow burns a few days old, cropping fresh shoots close to the ash. Patient handlers can tame them for meat and hides.", "RM_FE_Plant_ScorchFruit": "A woody seed-pod, sealed shut and inert until fire cracks its casing. Once cracked it ripens almost instantly on the heat alone \u2014 and goes soft and worthless again within a day if nothing picks it.", "RM_FE_Plant_EmberGrass": "A coarse bunchgrass that regrows on burned gro[bridge split] 0.1 s wall: load 0.0 / ticks 0.0 / reads 0.0 / other 0.0 / outside calls 0.1 s
und in a day or two. Its tall stems dry to dull orange almost as quickly, laying fresh tinder over the ash before grazers can clear it.", "RM_FlamefangVenom": "A burning venom from a flamefang's bite. It does not spread like an infection so much as smolder in place, a coal lodged under the skin \u2014 hot, slow, and worse the longer it sits untreated.", "RM_Pyrelands": "A hot, wind-scoured savanna, genetically engineered in a forgotten age to feed grazing herds, that has gone on burning on a schedule of its own for millennia. Coarse fast grass carpets the ground again within days of a burn, dries out soon after, and goes up at the first dry-storm strike. What is left behind is ash: drifting on every wind, falling in grey storms, banking into drifts, and lying deep over all of it. Dry, the ash is fair ground that takes a crop well enough, though the heat stunts it; wherever water reaches it, the ash turns very fertile, wet roots shrug off the heat and it grows almost anything. For a few days after a burn the ash itself feeds a field, and black rain on a fresh burn feeds it richer still. The rare rain here is black with it. Little grows tall enough to matter, so the horizon is nothing but grass, scars and smoke."}
